<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36534" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plāgōsus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>full of blows.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>fond of flogging</i>
				(<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Orbilius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 2, 1, 70</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Pass.</i>, <i>full</i>
			
			<i>of blows</i> or <i>wounds</i>
			(post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dorsum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 9, p. 222, 27</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crura,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 8</span></i>
			, p. 203, 17.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
